From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:50:37 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] kms: Support asynchronous page flips

Query DRM_CAP_ASYNC_PAGE_FLIP and DRM_CAP_ATOMIC_ASYNC_PAGE_FLIP and
expose the one matching the KMS mode as
meta_kms_device_supports_async_page_flip().

An update can now ask for an asynchronous flip with
meta_kms_update_set_async_flip(). Such an update skips the deadline
timer (it is committed as soon as it is ready, or as soon as the
previous flip completed) and is committed with DRM_MODE_PAGE_FLIP_ASYNC:

 - atomic: when the driver has the atomic cap and the update only
   changes primary plane buffers (no mode set, connector, CRTC, color,
   cursor or overlay plane changes, which atomic async commits cannot
   carry); a commit the driver refuses is retried synchronously.
 - legacy: drmModePageFlip with DRM_MODE_PAGE_FLIP_ASYNC when the driver
   has the cap, retried synchronously when refused.

Anything else falls back to a normal vertical blank synchronized flip.
The feedback of an update says whether it was flipped asynchronously
(meta_kms_feedback_is_async_flip()).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
